{
  "format": 1,
  "name": "port_developers_terrain_grid",
  "spec": ["port-developers 4.8", "port-developers 10"],
  "description": "The seaport's terrain grid (4.8, PD4, PD6; never runs with shipped data). A seaport type with a 3 x 2 grid (rows 3, columns 2, values 1..6, row-major). The use test compares only the product R x C = 6 with (x2 - x1)(z2 - z1) of the inclusive rectangle: a 4 x 3-cell lot (0,0)-(3,2) walks z = 0..1 (outer) and x = 0..2 (inner), the last row and column excluded. Facing 0: row = x - x1, column = z - z1 (rows along x); facing 2 is its 180-degree turn; facings 1 and 3 transpose (1: row = z2 - 1 - z, column = x2 - 1 - x; 3: row = z - z1, column = x - x1; the flat index row x 2 + column runs over the 3 x 2 grid [quirk]); any other facing sets nothing; a 3 x 3-cell lot (walk 4) is left alone. The write passes trunc(CellCenterToPosition) = ((x + 0.5) x 16, (z + 0.5) x 16) metres to SetAltitude as vertex indices [quirk]. On a 20 x 20-cell terrain (21 x 21 vertices) the z = 1 row (index 21 x 24 + x >= 441) is skipped [choice], while (40, 8) is written because its index 21 x 8 + 40 is inside the vertex array.",
